// Secrets.xcconfig.example — COMMITTED template. Contains NO real values.
//
// Setup:
//   cp Secrets.xcconfig.example Secrets.xcconfig
//   …then paste your real keys into Secrets.xcconfig (which is gitignored).
//
// Never put a real key in THIS file, and never commit Secrets.xcconfig.
//
// The three keys below flow: this file → the app target's baseConfigurationReference →
// Info.plist $(VAR) entries → Bundle.main.object(forInfoDictionaryKey:) in Store/Telemetry.
// A blank or placeholder value reads as "unset": the SDK is never configured, and a fresh
// clone stays silent (no purchases, no analytics) instead of spamming errors.

// RevenueCat PUBLIC SDK key for the "Airline Architect" App Store app (starts "appl_"). It's a
// client key (safe in a shipped binary), but it still doesn't belong in git. Left as this
// placeholder, in-app purchases stay disabled and the SDK is never configured — the paywall
// renders on its fallback prices and says nothing can be bought. Find it in the RevenueCat
// dashboard under the App Store app configuration ▸ Public API Key.
REVENUECAT_API_KEY = appl_replace_with_your_revenuecat_key

// RevenueCat TEST STORE key for the same project (starts "test_"). Optional, DEBUG-only: used
// only when a Debug build is launched with -useTestStore, which points the SDK at RevenueCat's
// own Test Store instead of the App Store. That is the ONLY way to complete a real purchase —
// and watch the entitlement actually flip isPro — in the SIMULATOR (the DEV Pro toggle bypasses
// every line of RevenueCat, so it proves only the gate, not the purchase path).
//
// It needs no Apple Developer membership, no App Store Connect app, no Paid Apps Agreement and
// no sandbox Apple Account — the Test Store is selected by this key's "test_" prefix and nothing
// else. Find it in the RevenueCat dashboard under Apps ▸ Test Store ▸ Show key.
//
// ⚠️ NEVER put a test_ key in REVENUECAT_API_KEY: the SDK fatalErrors on a test_ key in a
// Release build. It belongs here, and only ever in the gitignored Secrets.xcconfig.
REVENUECAT_TEST_API_KEY = test_replace_with_your_revenuecat_test_store_key

// TelemetryDeck app ID for the "Airline Architect" app in the TelemetryDeck dashboard. A
// client-side WRITE key (safe in a binary), routed the same way as the RevenueCat keys rather
// than hardcoded. Left as this placeholder, Telemetry.configure() declines to initialize the
// SDK at all, so a keyless clone is silent by design.
//
// Debug builds land in the dashboard's TEST DATA view (the SDK's testMode defaults to #if DEBUG);
// Release builds go live.
TELEMETRYDECK_APP_ID = your_telemetrydeck_app_id_here
